---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Shifting Supply Chain Analysts From Admin to Strategy - Marker">
  <Navbar />
  <main id="main-content">
    <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-16 md:pt-24 md:pb-24">
      <a href="/case-studies" class="mb-8 inline-flex items-center text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">
        <svg class="mr-1 h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"></path>
        </svg>
        All Case Studies
      </a>

      <span class="mb-3 inline-block text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">DTC Footwear</span>
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground md:text-3xl">Shifting Supply Chain Analysts From Admin to Strategy</h1>

      <div class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted/50 p-5 text-sm">
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Company</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Direct-to-consumer footwear brand with factories in Europe and Asia</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Team</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Supply chain analyst responsible for vendor relationships, cost management, and operational execution</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="block font-medium text-foreground">Key Challenge</span>
            <span class="text-muted-foreground">Analyst's time consumed by invoice reconciliation, payment tracking, and return processing — leaving no bandwidth for cost optimization or vendor strategy</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Challenge</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">The supply chain analyst at this DTC footwear brand described a daily reality dominated by administrative work: reconciling invoices against PO terms, tracking payment status across vendors with different terms (net 90 for European factories, deposit plus net 60 for Asian suppliers), processing returns, and verifying factory invoices line by line. With 6 product categories and growing, the volume of administrative tasks scaled faster than the team.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">The work the analyst wanted to focus on — evaluating new vendor options, optimizing shipping costs (the difference between air at $3.50-5.50 per pair and ocean at under $2 per pair from Europe was significant at scale), and improving the customer experience — was perpetually deferred. Every hour spent checking whether a factory invoice matched the PO was an hour not spent on strategic work that could meaningfully improve the business.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">The challenge was compounded by a 5-7 month concept-to-shelf timeline: when administrative overhead causes delays, the entire product calendar shifts, and recovery time is measured in months, not days.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">The Approach</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Marker automates the administrative tasks that consume the analyst's day. When a factory sends an invoice, Marker cross-references it against the relevant PO terms — checking quantities, unit prices, payment terms, and shipping charges. Discrepancies are flagged with the specific line items that don't match, eliminating the need for line-by-line manual verification.</p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Payment terms are tracked per vendor: Marker knows which vendors expect net 90, which require deposits, and when payments are due. Ship date updates are surfaced alongside cost implications — if air shipping becomes necessary due to a delay, the cost impact is calculated automatically. For the analyst, this means the administrative layer of the job runs in the background, surfacing only the exceptions that need human judgment. The freed-up time goes directly into the strategic work the analyst was hired to do.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-10">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-foreground">Key Takeaways</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-muted-foreground">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Invoice-to-PO reconciliation automated, with only discrepancies surfaced for human review</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Payment terms tracked per vendor with due dates and status visible in one place</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Cost implications of delays calculated automatically — including shipping mode changes and their financial impact</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
            <span class="mt-1.5 block h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span>Analyst time redirected from invoice checking and payment tracking to vendor evaluation and cost optimization</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-12 rounded-lg border border-primary/20 bg-primary/5 p-6 text-center">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-foreground">See how Marker frees your supply chain team to focus on strategy, not admin.</p>
        <a href="/book-demo" class="mt-4 inline-flex h-10 items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary px-6 text-sm font-medium text-primary-foreground transition-colors hover:bg-primary/90 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2">Book a Demo</a>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
